Now it is time for my lunch.
I go outside the office.
The street is very crowded.
A tourist is standing there.
He has a map in his hand.
He looks very lost.
He comes over to me.
He asks, "Excuse me, Madam."
"Where is the big post office here?"
I smile.
I know the way.
I say, "Please go straight from here."
"There is a big intersection ahead."
"Please turn left from there."
"The big post office is on the right side."
The tourist looks at the place on the map.
He becomes happy.
He says, "Thank you very much, Madam."
I say, "No problem."
He goes towards the post office.
